'fill in'. Documentation fields after @ are especially strong; backslash
commands, markup tags, printf letters, and ellipses are weaker signals.
Split Unicode tokens are classified by the character they complete, with
stronger responses to spaced symbols and Greek letters than Asian text.
Numbered chapter/article suffixes also receive a positive response.

