The component fires on the word (or word-piece) of a token that names doing arithmetic or
quantitative estimation: "calculate", "estimated", "compute", "count", "account", "measure",
"statistics", "budget", "approximately", and their Chinese and Japanese counterparts (计, 計,
计算, 估计, 合计, 预算). Weaker on the words that often precede or describe such work
("plan", "design", "total", "amount", "analysis", "how", "some"). The program scores the
current token by how strongly it names quantitative work, and is 0 for everything else.
Each word is read from its own text, so it needs no context beyond the current token.
